Hi Antonio,

Thank you for your answer, I understand it but I'm trying to do it for an undirected graph so I have to map  from and to nodes as keys.

I'm trying to do it with the following code, with no outputs errors  but the file is returned empty and don't know why.

What am I doing wrong? I'm not sure that I can put keyval() in a for loop can I?

 map <- function(k,v) {
fields <- unlist(strsplit(v, "\t"))

nodes <- unique(c(fields[1],fields[2]))
  for (l in nodes){
  if( any(aux<-which(fields[1]==l))){my_v=fields[2][aux]}else if(any(aux1<-which(fields[2]==l))){my_v=fields[1][aux1]}
  keyval(l,my_v)

  }
}

reduce <- function(k,vv) {
  keyval(k, (unlist(vv)))
}

kvtextoutputformat = function(k,v) {
  paste(c(k,v, "\n"), collapse = "\t")
}

mapreduce(
 input = "Tests.txt",
 output = "output-RHadoop",
 #textinputformat = rawtextinputformat,
 #textoutputformat = kvtextoutputformat,
 output.format='text',
 map = map,
 reduce = reduce)

Thanks

